{"content_hash": "6ef4c617651b35d3", "version_id": 146, "article_id": 15, "level_code": "ja_n5", "lang": "ja", "level": 1, "level_label": "N5 初級", "title": "アメリカの死刑囚、クリスタ・パイクさんが話す", "title_zh": "美国死刑犯克里斯塔·派克还能说话", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8kgezxn54qko?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/226c/live/7221efd0-c1c9-11f1-b8a9-47f21beea0a3.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 242, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "アメリカのテネシー州で、死刑の注射がうまくいきませんでした。クリスタ・パイクさんは生きています。今、話すことができます。", "lead_zh": "在美国田纳西州，注射死刑没执行成功。克里斯塔·派克活了下来。现在她能说话了。", "preview": "パイクさんは50歳です。1995年、19歳の女性を殺しました。それで死刑になりました。先週の水曜日、テネシー州で注射をしました。でも、2回とも失敗しました。", "preview_zh": "派克今年50岁。1995年，她杀了一名19岁的女性。因此被判死刑。上周三，在田纳西州给她注射。但是两次都失败了。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 136, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@d7bba21/content/audio/15/ja_n5.mp3", "duration": 58.275, "size_bytes": 353376, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 176, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@d7bba21/content/data/versions/146.json", "paragraphs": ["パイクさんは50歳です。1995年、19歳の女性を殺しました。それで死刑になりました。先週の水曜日、テネシー州で注射をしました。でも、2回とも失敗しました。", "パイクさんは病院に運ばれました。何日も意識がありませんでした。医者が薬を体から出しました。今は意識があり、話します。手錠をつけられています。", "専門家は「とても珍しい」と言います。今まで、注射で生き残った人はいません。パイクさんだけです。なぜ失敗したか、まだわかりません。", "テネシー州の知事は、今年の死刑を止めました。刑務所の責任者は辞めます。パイクさんをまた死刑にするかは、まだ決まっていません。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["派克今年50岁。1995年，她杀了一名19岁的女性。因此被判死刑。上周三，在田纳西州给她注射。但是两次都失败了。", "派克被送到医院。好几天没有意识。医生把药物从她体内排出去。现在她有意识，能说话。她戴着手铐。", "专家说“非常罕见”。到现在为止，没有人注射后活下来。只有派克。为什么失败，还不知道。", "田纳西州州长停止了今年的死刑。监狱负责人要辞职。是否再次对派克执行死刑，还没有决定。"], "body": "パイクさんは50歳です。1995年、19歳の女性を殺しました。それで死刑になりました。先週の水曜日、テネシー州で注射をしました。でも、2回とも失敗しました。\n\nパイクさんは病院に運ばれました。何日も意識がありませんでした。医者が薬を体から出しました。今は意識があり、話します。手錠をつけられています。\n\n専門家は「とても珍しい」と言います。今まで、注射で生き残った人はいません。パイクさんだけです。なぜ失敗したか、まだわかりません。\n\nテネシー州の知事は、今年の死刑を止めました。刑務所の責任者は辞めます。パイクさんをまた死刑にするかは、まだ決まっていません。", "body_zh": "派克今年50岁。1995年，她杀了一名19岁的女性。因此被判死刑。上周三，在田纳西州给她注射。但是两次都失败了。\n\n派克被送到医院。好几天没有意识。医生把药物从她体内排出去。现在她有意识，能说话。她戴着手铐。\n\n专家说“非常罕见”。到现在为止，没有人注射后活下来。只有派克。为什么失败，还不知道。\n\n田纳西州州长停止了今年的死刑。监狱负责人要辞职。是否再次对派克执行死刑，还没有决定。", "text": "パイクさんは50歳です。1995年、19歳の女性を殺しました。それで死刑になりました。先週の水曜日、テネシー州で注射をしました。でも、2回とも失敗しました。 パイクさんは病院に運ばれました。何日も意識がありませんでした。医者が薬を体から出しました。今は意識があり、話します。手錠をつけられています。 専門家は「とても珍しい」と言います。今まで、注射で生き残った人はいません。パイクさんだけです。なぜ失敗したか、まだわかりません。 テネシー州の知事は、今年の死刑を止めました。刑務所の責任者は辞めます。パイクさんをまた死刑にするかは、まだ決まっていません。", "vocab": [{"word": "死刑", "pos": "noun", "zh": "死刑", "note": "しけい"}, {"word": "注射", "pos": "noun", "zh": "注射", "note": "ちゅうしゃ"}, {"word": "失敗", "pos": "noun", "zh": "失败", "note": "しっぱい"}, {"word": "病院", "pos": "noun", "zh": "医院", "note": "びょういん"}, {"word": "意識", "pos": "noun", "zh": "意识", "note": "いしき"}, {"word": "専門家", "pos": "noun", "zh": "专家", "note": "せんもんか"}, {"word": "知事", "pos": "noun", "zh": "州长", "note": "ちじ"}, {"word": "辞める", "pos": "verb", "zh": "辞职", "note": "やめる"}], "title_original": "US death row inmate Christa Pike awake and speaking after failed execution, lawyers say", "summary_original": "Experts and lawyers called the apparent recovery unprecedented, noting she is believed to be the only known person to survive a lethal injection.", "body_original": "US death row inmate Christa Pike awake and speaking after failed execution, lawyers say\nBy\nSareen Habeshian\nand\nKwasi Gyamfi Asiedu\nPublished\n6 October 2026\nUpdated 57 minutes ago\nUS death row inmate Christa Pike is \"conscious and speaking\" after surviving a failed execution attempt last week, her lawyers say.\nPike, 50, continues to receive critical medical care while handcuffed in hospital, her attorneys said in a statement on Tuesday.\nPike, who was sentenced to death after murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995, survived two failed lethal injections last Wednesday in Tennessee. She was taken to hospital, where she remained unconscious for days as medical staff cleared her body of the injected chemical.\nExperts and her legal team say her apparent recovery is unprecedented. She is believed to be the only person to survive a lethal injection.\nHer lawyers called her progress \"medically unprecedented\", and while her prognosis remains unclear, \"at a minimum, we expect a long recovery\".\nDeborah Denno, a criminologist and professor at Fordham Law School, said she was \"absolutely astonished\" that Pike is conscious and speaking.\nThere were seven other cases where prisoners survived slated executions, but in those cases, executioners were not able to inject anything into the inmates' veins, Denno told the BBC.\nPike \"is the only person for whom some kind of toxin has been injected,\" she said.\n\"They did everything they were supposed to do as part of the execution process, and it simply didn't work,\" Denno said. \"This has never happened before.\"\nAuthorities have not yet said whether they will try again to execute Pike. They have also not offered an explanation for what went wrong after injecting her with the chemical pentobarbital.\nTennessee Governor Bill Lee suspended all executions for the rest of the year - and the head of prisons in the state said over the weekend that he plans to resign.\nPike was 18 when she and her then-boyfriend, Tadaryl Shipp, beat, tortured and killed 19-year-old Slemmer, whom they had met at a job training camp for troubled teens.\nPike's attorneys are scheduled to appear in court in Nashville on Wednesday. They also plan to hold a news conference outside the court.\nDr Joel Zivot, an anaesthesiologist advising Pike's defence team, said on Tuesday that the likelihood of recovering from lethal injection is low.\n\"Most people who get lethal injection die from it,\" he told the BBC. \"In fact, pretty well everyone, except Christa. So, the fact that she survived it ... was unusual.\"\nBut there remains a lot of uncertainty and many unknowns, he said, including how much of the pentobarbital got into her system, what her blood levels were after the injection and what her recovery will look like.\n\"I would not, in any way, say at this point that all the big risks are behind her,\" he noted.\nZivot had previously said the two doses of pentobarbital she received last week would have been enough that, had it entered her bloodstream in normal circulation, \"she would have surely died\".\nInstead, Zivot said a possible explanation is that instead of entering Pike's bloodstream, the pentobarbital was more likely to have spread across the tissue under her skin.\nZivot said last week he thought her ending up with a brain injury was \"very possible\", due to the delays in resuscitating her. He also believed it would take about a week to truly understand her condition and do a neurological exam. It's now been six days since the failed attempt to execute her.\nPike's lawyers previously warned that her medical history and anatomy - including thrombocytosis (a blood-clotting condition) and small veins - meant there was a risk she would experience \"unnecessary\" pain and suffering during a lethal injection.\nThey said on Tuesday that she has endured \"severe damage\" to her arms.\nRelated topics\nTennessee\nCapital punishment\nUnited States\nMore on this story\nI interviewed Christa Pike 20 years ago - I can't stop thinking about her\nPublished\n3 days ago\nTennessee prison chief to resign after Christa Pike's failed execution\nPublished\n3 days ago\nWhat happened in the failed execution of Christa Pike - and what next?\nPublished\nJust now", "fetched_at": "2026-10-07T00:57:05.204052", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "パイク", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.45, "sm": 125, "em": 450, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "さん", "s": 0.463, "e": 0.713, "sm": 462, "em": 712, "cs": 3, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "は", "s": 0.725, "e": 0.875, "sm": 725, "em": 875, "cs": 5, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "50", "s": 0.9, "e": 1.308, "sm": 900, "